# act configuration — WORKFLOW WIRING SMOKE TEST ONLY.
#
# act runs GitHub workflows locally against substitute runner images. It is
# useful for exactly one thing here: catching a broken workflow before it costs
# hosted minutes to discover. YAML that does not parse, a job that depends on an
# output that is never set, an `if:` that never fires, a shell syntax error.
#
# It is NOT evidence for:
#   * Windows replay parity        - act cannot run the Windows runner at all
#   * numerical parity with hosted - substitute images, different wheels
#   * runtime or billing figures   - different hardware entirely
#   * clean-room independence      - it runs on your machine, against your tree
#
# The Docker CI in ci/ remains the local model-test authority. See ci/README.md.

# Medium image: has python and the common tooling, without the ~20GB full image.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

# Apple silicon and some Windows/WSL setups need this to run amd64 images.
--container-architecture linux/amd64

# Reuse containers between runs so an iteration on the YAML is seconds.
--reuse

# Keep act's artifacts out of the tracked tree.
--artifact-server-path /tmp/act-artifacts
